# Sample files

When a change affects what this app saves or how a website renders it, update the matching sample in the same change.

- `samples/bynder-field-large-hero.json`, `samples/bynder-field-split-left-right.json`, and `samples/bynder-field-custom.json` — one custom field value each (`v`, `profile`, `assets`), not a Contentstack entry. Same Bynder files, different profile snapshots. The custom file uses `profile.id` `"custom"`. Match `persistedPayload` in `src/lib/settings.ts`. Leave out keys the app no longer writes, including asset `aspectRatio`, `zoom`, and a top-level `profileSettings`. Keep the existing sample assets unless the new shape needs an example they do not cover.
- `samples/BynderPicture.tsx` — a React `<picture>` for the largeHero payload. It must keep using `buildBynderSources` for the DAT URLs. The request uses each viewport `targetWidth` and the height from its aspect ratio, and neither side may pass `maxDimension` (2000 when the snapshot omits it). Update this file when delivery, srcset steps, the max dimension, or the picture markup changes. Leave it alone for editor-only work.
- `samples/bynder-picture-large-hero.html`, `samples/bynder-picture-split-left-right.html`, and `samples/bynder-picture-custom.html` — one `<picture>` each, with the URLs filled in for the matching payload. largeHero uses `sizes="100vw"`. splitLeftRight uses `sizes="40vw"`. custom uses `sizes="100vw"`. `img` `width` and `height` are that picture's desktop request size, not the CSS size. `sizes` is the displayed width. Keep the HTML comment at the top of each file. Write query separators as `&`, not `&amp;`. Regenerate a file whenever its payload or the picture markup changes. Do not add a full document around the picture.

Do not fork the URL math into the sample.
